    },
    {
      "id": "IRCH1-RESTORE-EXPECTATIONS",
      "severity": "none",
      "status": "pass",
      "text": "The restore assertions align with the existing relocated-history control: four revisions remain historical, live project export is refused with LIGHT_WORKSPACE_MISMATCH, and a copied missing-HEAD project is the intended backup conflict fixture. Backup should not infer a blocker merely from valid partial prose; the fixture records the explicit missing/edited HEAD condition."
    },
    {
      "id": "IRCH1-OUTPUT-PATH",
      "severity": "major",
      "status": "precondition",
      "text": "The integrated CLI requires backup/archive, restore destination, and Markdown output paths under .work/**. The operator must pass --output as a fresh invocation directory under .work and outside the source workspace; an artifacts/** output path or a pre-existing output directory will fail before the replay assertions."
    },
    {
      "id": "IRCH1-WRITING-AWARE-BACKUP",
      "severity": "major",
      "status": "precondition",
      "text": "The pending-publication refusal depends on the integrated light_backup.py calling writing_backup_blockers. The T2 stopped light_backup.py snapshot itself has no writing hook, while the T3 working copy does; the stopped integrated candidate must carry the exact writing-aware backup integration before this harness can claim the expected LIGHT_BACKUP_CONFLICT."
    },
    {
      "id": "IRCH1-RESTORED-BACKUP-ASSERTION",
      "severity": "minor",
      "status": "gap",
      "text": "backup.restored-history is called with the default success expectation, but the harness does not assert its payload is ok, that the archive exists, or that the archive verifies. A false positive is possible if this command returns an unexpected success-shaped payload or creates no usable archive."
    },
    {
      "id": "IRCH1-BATCH-STATUS-SHAPE",
      "severity": "minor",
      "status": "gap",
      "text": "Batch-status calls are required to return ok/exit 0 but no expected status, completeness, accepted-count, or missing-batch fields are asserted in the harness; report collection alone could admit a semantically degraded status if the CLI ever returns ok true with incomplete fields."
    },
    {
      "id": "IRCH1-ERROR-REPORTING",
      "severity": "minor",
      "status": "gap",
      "text": "call() parses stdout as JSON and raises on malformed/empty output; only ProbeFailure is caught by main. A CLI transport regression can therefore escape as an unstructured traceback from the harness instead of a report.json with passed=false."
    },
    {
      "id": "IRCH1-SCOPE",
      "severity": "none",
      "status": "pass",
      "text": "The script is a replay of existing exported documents and trial state, sets human_scientific_acceptance false, and independently rechecks PDFs, notes, writing bytes, restore history, and pending-backup immutability."
    }
